1. A method for producing tofu, comprising:
a grinding step of grinding a first mixture of soybeans and water until a volume-based median diameter in a particle size distribution of the soybeans in the first mixture, measured by a dynamic light scattering method, becomes 250 μm or less;
a heating step of heating the ground first mixture;
a separating step of separating the ground and heated first mixture into soymilk and okara; and
a coagulating step of preparing tofu by coagulating a second mixture of the soymilk and a coagulant.
